```java
public class SearchAlgorithm {
  public int search(int[] array, int target) {
    int left = 0;
    int right = array.length - 1;

    while (left <= right) {
      int mid = (left + right) / 2;

      if (array[mid] == target) {
        return mid;
      }

      // Determine which side is sorted
      if (array[left] <= array[mid]) {  // Left side is sorted
        if (array[left] <= target && target < array[mid]) {
          right = mid - 1;
        } else {
          left = mid + 1;
        }
      } else {  // Right side is sorted
        if (array[mid] < target && target <= array[right]) {
          left = mid + 1;
        } else {
          right = mid - 1;
        }
      }
    }
    return -1;
  }

  public static void main(String[] args) {
    SearchAlgorithm sa = new SearchAlgorithm();
    int[] rotatedArray = {4, 5, 6, 7, 0, 1, 2};
    System.out.println(sa.search(rotatedArray, 0));  // Output: 4
    System.out.println(sa.search(rotatedArray, 3));  // Output: -1
  }
}
```

This code implements a search algorithm for a rotated sorted array, maintaining a time complexity of O(log n). The `main` method includes test cases to demonstrate the functionality.

